[{:db/id "q-350940/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "af1258a6-8a9f-5108-955d-fb5228710cf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350940/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "11f58b7f-9636-5b63-ad91-203ed10257e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350940/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c43d5216-bdea-5199-98d0-80b683f15a24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350940/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-350940/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-350940/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350940/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "4bd503f3-e108-5605-a285-fe505d0132b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350940/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7113323a-e369-532c-89f4-ae7e995aa587" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350940/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-350940/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350940" :question/id #uuid "a8a64fcd-2ae3-54d6-ab3a-f736d8506ae6" :question/math-academy-id "q-350940" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{4-5x}{x(x-1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{4-5x}{x(x-1)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x$ |  | $x-1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-5x}{x(x-1)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $x(x-1)$ gives\n\n$$\n4-5x=A(x-1)+Bx.\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-5(0) & =A(0-1)+B(0) \\\\ 4 & =-A \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-5(1) & =A(1-1)+B(1) \\\\ -1 & =B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-5x}{x(x-1)}=\\frac{-4}{x}+\\frac{-1}{x-1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-350940/field-1" "q-350940/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350940"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350934/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c750b503-d761-5306-9a48-199a0a56b4bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350934/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ac06ac1-0ed5-5d6c-a4da-a335243c819e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350934/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-350934/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350934" :question/id #uuid "d5c75d54-5a8a-5074-ad31-4334e1979979" :question/math-academy-id "q-350934" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{5x+11}{(x+1)(x+3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{5x+11}{(x+1)(x+3)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+1$ |  | $x+3$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+11}{(x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{x+1}+\\frac{2}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+1)(x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n5x+11=A(x+3)+2(x+1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-1)+11 & =A(-1+3)+2(-1+1) \\\\ 6 & =2A \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+11}{(x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac{3}{x+1}+\\frac{2}{x+3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-350934/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350934"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350968/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c22605db-cac2-5f94-a4d4-efb7e6ccde60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350968/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "22a4fbed-f5e0-555a-bdb7-17286fb56373" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350968/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-350968/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350968/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "278fa2c3-0329-5131-a0f1-b1d31436680f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350968/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e6cec30-eea3-56fe-80a6-984171756381" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350968/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-350968/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350968/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "29ea2a58-8b1e-5d43-aab8-a144acbd6833" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350968/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "976ab995-8544-573b-95bb-64062fc38295" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350968/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-350968/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350968" :question/id #uuid "06babcd4-bbb4-5621-bb1f-d33fa0f96d00" :question/math-academy-id "q-350968" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-2$ |  | $x+1$ |  | $3x+4$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{x+1}+\\frac{C}{3x+4}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)$ gives\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+19x+30=A(x+1)(3x+4)+B(x-2)(3x+4)+C(x-2)(x+1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(2)^{2}+19(2)+30 & =A(2+1)(3(2)+4)+B(2-2)(3(2)+4)+C(2-2)(2+1) \\\\ 60 & =30A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(-1)^{2}+19(-1)+30 & =A(-1+1)(3(-1)+4)+B(-1-2)(3(-1)+4)+C(-1-2)(-1+1) \\\\ 9 & =-3B \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{4}{3}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{(-\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}+19(-\\frac{4}{3})+30 & =A(-\\frac{4}{3}+1)(3(-\\frac{4}{3})+4) \\\\  & \\,\\,+B(-\\frac{4}{3}-2)(3(-\\frac{4}{3})+4) \\\\  & \\,\\,+C(-\\frac{4}{3}-2)(-\\frac{4}{3}+1) \\\\ \\frac{10}{9} & =\\frac{10}{9}C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}=\\frac{2}{x-2}-\\frac{3}{x+1}+\\frac{1}{3x+4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-350968/field-1" "q-350968/field-2" "q-350968/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350968"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-10989"] :question/problem "Express $\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+21x+41}{(x+1)(2-x)(x+3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+21x+41}{(x+1)(2-x)(x+3)} & =\\frac{A}{(x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(2-x)}+\\frac{C}{(x+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+1)(2-x)(x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+21x+41=A(2-x)(x+3)+B(x+1)(x+3)+C(x+1)(2-x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(-1)^{2}+21(-1)+41 & =A(2-(-1))(-1+3) \\\\  & \\,+B(-1+1)(-1+3) \\\\  & +C(-1+1)(2-(-1)) \\\\ -2-21+41 & =A(6) \\\\ A & =\\frac{18}{6} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=2$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(2)^{2}+21(2)+41 & =A(2-2)(2+3) \\\\  & \\,+B(2+1)(2+3) \\\\  & +C(2+1)(2-2) \\\\ -8+42+41 & =B(15) \\\\ B & =\\frac{75}{15} \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(-3)^{2}+21(-3)+41 & =A(2-(-3))(-3+3) \\\\  & \\,+B(-3+1)(-3+3) \\\\  & +C(-3+1)(2-(-3)) \\\\ -18-63+41 & =C(-10) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-40}{-10} \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+21x+41}{(x+1)(2-x)(x+3)}=\\frac{3}{(x+1)}+\\frac{5}{(2-x)}+\\frac{4}{(x+3)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-351007/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9df0cbe6-3751-5c6f-b437-9d62124b3bd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351007/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "861df757-d51b-59b9-98cb-e060221974ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351007/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-351007/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351007/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "34310332-fd54-5749-8b6f-d5a6212339ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351007/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "620ec75e-9986-557c-be41-110ca7dd7d1b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351007/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-351007/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351007/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "81425749-b638-5f9c-bd20-e55d0ec93a44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351007/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b65804c-836c-5633-b753-a23cc13ed14f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351007/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-351007/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351007" :question/id #uuid "4f3ed87d-5ab6-56a5-bf4e-dbbffa2cf3fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-351007" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} | $-$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2x+1$ |  | $3x-4$ |  | $x-2$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}=\\frac{A}{2x+1}+\\frac{B}{3x-4}+\\frac{C}{x-2}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)$ gives\n\n$$\n18-19x=A(3x-4)(x-2)+B(2x+1)(x-2)+C(2x+1)(3x-4).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18-19(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =A(3(-\\frac{1}{2})-4)(-\\frac{1}{2}-2) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(-\\frac{1}{2}-2) \\\\  & \\,+C(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(3(-\\frac{1}{2})-4) \\\\ \\frac{55}{2} & =\\frac{55}{4}A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{4}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18-19(\\frac{4}{3}) & =A(3(\\frac{4}{3})-4)(\\frac{4}{3}-2) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(\\frac{4}{3})+1)(\\frac{4}{3}-2) \\\\  & \\,+C(2(\\frac{4}{3})+1)(3(\\frac{4}{3})-4) \\\\ -\\frac{22}{3} & =-\\frac{22}{9}B \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18-19(2) & =A(3(2)-4)(2-2)+B(2(2)+1)(2-2)+C(2(2)+1)(3(2)-4) \\\\ -20 & =10C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}=\\frac{2}{2x+1}+\\frac{3}{3x-4}-\\frac{2}{x-2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-351007/field-1" "q-351007/field-2" "q-351007/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351007"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-10981"] :question/problem "Express $\\frac{16{x}^{2}+55x+19}{(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16{x}^{2}+55x+19}{(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)} & =\\frac{A}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n16{x}^{2}+55x+19=A(x+5)(x+1)+B(2x+1)(x+1)+C(2x+1)(x+5).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+55(-\\frac{1}{2})+19 & =A(-\\frac{1}{2}+5)(-\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & +B(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(-\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(-\\frac{1}{2}+5) \\\\ 4-\\frac{55}{2}+19 & =A(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{46-55}{2} & =A(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ A & =\\frac{-36}{18} \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16(-5)^{2}+55(-5)+19 & =A(-5+5)(-5+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-5)+1)(-5+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-5)+1)(-5+5) \\\\ 400-275+19 & =B((-9)(-4)) \\\\ B & =\\frac{144}{36} \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16(-1)^{2}+55(-1)+19 & =A(-1+5)(-1+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-1)+1)(-1+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-1)+1)(-1+5) \\\\ 16-55+19 & =C(-4) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-20}{-4} \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{16{x}^{2}+55x+19}{(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)}=-\\frac{2}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{4}{(x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x+1)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-501"] :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x-3)}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above expression through by $(x+2)(x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n2x-1= A(x-3)+B(x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ term and allows us to solve for $A.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)-1 & =A(-2-3)+B(-2+2) \\\\ -5 & =A(-5)+B(0) \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ term and allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3)-1 & =A(3-3)+B(3+2) \\\\ 5 & =A(0)+B(5) \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1$ and $B=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{1}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{1}{(x-3)}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-502"] :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{x+2} + \\dfrac{B}{x-3} + \\dfrac{C}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply both sides of the equation by $(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)$ to clear the fractions:\n\n$$\n2x^2+5x+7= A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+2)(x+1)+C(x+2)(x-3)\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $A.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)^{2}+5(-2)+7 & =A(-2-3)(-2+1) \\\\ 5 & =A(5) \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $B.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3)^{2}+5(3)+7 & =B(3+2)(3+1) \\\\ 40 & =B(20) \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, plugging in $x=-1$ gets rid of the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)^{2}+5(-1)+7 & =C(-1+2)(-1-3) \\\\ 4 & =C(-4) \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1,$ $B=2,$ and $C=-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{1}{x+2} +\\dfrac{2}{x-3} -\\dfrac{1}{x+1}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
